{"ticker":"NAVINFLUOR","symbol":"NAVINFLUOR","instrumentId":3023076,"name":"Navin Fluorine Intl.","industry":"NSE-Chemicals-Specialty","about":"Navin Fluorine International Ltd. operates across four main business segments: fluorochemicals, specialty chemicals, CRAMS, and inorganic fluorides. The company's fluorochemicals are used in refrigeration and air conditioning systems, while their specialty chemicals support industries like pharmaceuticals and agrochemicals. The CRAMS segment provides contract research and manufacturing services, primarily to global pharma and biotech companies, offering expertise in chemical processes and complex molecules. Additionally, Navin Fluorine supplies inorganic fluorides, which are crucial in metallurgical applications. The company has a global presence and serves various industries by providing high-quality, specialized chemical solutions.","website":"www.nfil.in","location":"Sion East, INDIA","exchange":"NSE","fetchedAt":"2026-11-20T13:43:40.463Z","basis":"consolidated","price":{"value":10203,"changePct":-0.7297139521307647,"week52High":10278,"week52Low":5563},"stats":[{"label":"Market capitalization","value":"₹52,374 Cr"},{"label":"Sales","value":"₹4,066 Cr"},{"label":"Shares in float","value":"37,472,000"},{"label":"No. of funds","value":"438"},{"label":"Shares held by funds","value":"26,719,572"},{"label":"Dividend yield","value":"0.16%"},{"label":"Book value","value":"13.16"},{"label":"U/D vol ratio","value":"1.8"},{"label":"LTDebt / equity","value":"24.0%"},{"label":"Alpha","value":"0.24"},{"label":"Beta","value":"0.9"},{"label":"EPS growth rate","value":"19%"},{"label":"P/E ratio","value":"57.45"},{"label":"5-year P/E range","value":"48–86"},{"label":"Return on equity","value":"16.7%"},{"label":"Cash flow (INR)","value":"174.36"},{"label":"Volume","value":"297,254"},{"label":"Avg volume (50d)","value":"171,034"},{"label":"Master score","value":"81"},{"label":"EPS rating","value":"89"},{"label":"Price strength","value":"91"}